## Feature 2: User Access and Activity Monitoring

### Description
This security feature controls what each user can access in the inventory management system and keeps track of important activities performed by users.

### How the Feature Works
Each user is given an account with specific permissions based on their role. For example, a staff member may be allowed to view and update stock, while an administrator can add or remove users and manage system settings. The system also records important actions, such as stock updates or product deletions, so administrators can monitor activities and identify unauthorized or suspicious changes.
